## The four tabs

The KinderCare staff app is deliberately small. Everything lives behind four tabs along the bottom:

- **Activities** — what you record about the children through the day.
- **Students** — the children in your class.
- **Calendar** — events for your class.
- **Reports** — the written reports that go to parents.

There's no side drawer and no separate admin area to go looking for. If something isn't on one of
these four tabs, it isn't in this app.

{% callout type="note" %}
This is the teacher's app. Parents have a **separate** app with its own tabs — see
[The KinderCare Parent App](/docs/kindercare-parent-app). The two show much of the same information,
so it helps to know which one someone is describing before troubleshooting with them.
{% /callout %}

## Enrolling a child

**Students → Add Student** collects the child's details in grouped sections — personal information
(full name, student ID, date of birth), academic information, and contact information including the
address. You can attach a photo at the same time, taken with the **camera** or picked from the
**gallery**.

Students can be searched by name from the Students tab, which is usually faster than scrolling once
a class fills up.

## The calendar

The Calendar tab is editable, not just a view: you can **add**, **edit** and **delete** events.
Deleting asks for confirmation first, since parents may already have seen the event in their app.

## Account settings

**Account Settings** is intentionally minimal. Alongside your account details it offers **Request
Account Deletion** — a request to the school rather than something that happens immediately, so
submitting it does not sign you out or remove your records on the spot.

